  "limits": [
    "Raw-status cases assume the ISR has been entered. Disabled descriptor-error or done bits alone need not trigger a physical interrupt.",
    "Abnormal EOF is a GDMA event flag; this research does not establish which I2S/PDM hardware condition can produce it.",
    "The persistent-update-bit case stops after four synthetic reads of the same set bit. It establishes no timeout in that loop, not a measured hang or a bypass of watchdog behavior.",
    "GDMA reset/start/stop errors are injected at helper boundaries. Their physical reachability and peripheral outcome are unproven.",
    "Interrupt latency, scheduling, signal quality, eFuse configuration and actual frame recovery are not simulated."
  ]
